  "@type": "TargetCommunity",
  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who identify with or relate to the experience of procrastination, poor time management, and the humorous self-deprecation of failing to follow through on long-term personal goals. This includes people who have set New Year’s resolutions or yearly plans that they have not accomplished, and who find irony and humor in the concept of 'finally' doing something they promised themselves years ago. The meme appeals to a broad, relatable demographic across age groups who engage with self-improvement content, productivity culture, and internet humor centered on personal responsibility and goal-setting failures. The visual of the determined child serves as a universal symbol of resolve, making the meme accessible and funny to anyone who has felt the pressure to 'just do it' after years of delay.",
